From: mbt28 <btekbas@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] audio: 22 kHz on soft-float ARM

The OPL emulator (ADLIBEMU-derived) synthesizes the music in floating
point. On an ARM926 without an FPU at 44 kHz it cannot keep up: measured
on an F1C200s at 792 MHz, the 44.1 kHz mono stream sat in XRUN 46% of
the time (247 state changes in 10 s) with the audio thread at 45% CPU --
heavily distorted audio. Use 22 kHz there, as the GP2X/Dingux builds
already do; SAMPLE_SCALING follows, so the sound effects match.
---
--- a/src/loudness.h
+++ b/src/loudness.h
@@ -26,7 +26,11 @@
 
 #define SFX_CHANNELS 8
 
-#if defined(TARGET_GP2X) || defined(TARGET_DINGUX)
+/* 22 kHz on the handhelds and on any soft-float ARM (no FPU): the OPL
+ * emulator synthesizes the music in floating point, which cannot keep up
+ * with 44 kHz there -- constant underruns, heavily distorted audio. */
+#if defined(TARGET_GP2X) || defined(TARGET_DINGUX) || \
+    (defined(__arm__) && !defined(__ARM_FP))
 #define OUTPUT_QUALITY 2  // 22 kHz
 #else
 #define OUTPUT_QUALITY 4  // 44 kHz
